{"id": "b502023fd4c803c3", "title": "Nvidia Without Huang: What a Pause in AI Deals Means for Metals", "body": "Copper slid to its lowest in almost four months on Friday and was heading for a fifth straight weekly loss, with traders blaming Nvidia's (Nasdaq: NVDA) loss of Jensen Huang for the latest leg down. The exit is a convenient culprit, but the slide started before it. Copper has dropped every week since mid-October, and Goldman Sachs called the correction a matter of positioning in AI-linked stocks, not a sign that fundamentals have loosened. Three-month copper on the London Metal Exchange was down 0.5% at $13,519 a metric ton as of 1000 GMT,…", "link": "https://oilprice.com/Metals/Commodities/Nvidia-Without-Huang-What-a-Pause-in-AI-Deals-Means-for-Metals.html", "source": "oilprice", "group": "feeds_unverified", "weight": 7, "tags": ["oil"], "published_utc": "2026-11-14T22:00:00Z", "published_pkt": "15 Nov 03:00", "first_seen_pkt": "15 Nov 04:36", "trading_day": "2026-11-15"}
